  "reply_text": "Found one bug I’d fix before merging:\n\n**[P2] `topTags` mutates its input, breaking the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud before taking `tags.slice(0, 5)` (`src/render.js:4–5`), “recent” becomes the five most popular tags rather than the first five in the original order. This also violates the documented non-mutating helper contract.\n\nConfirmed with six tags: a popular tag originally last incorrectly appears first in “recent.” Sort a copy instead, and add regression tests for unchanged input and preserved recent order.\n\nAll **4 existing tests pass**, but none checks this behavior. Reviewed `main...tag-cloud`; no files changed.",
